This problem setup is to test the ability of ERF to correctly use 
initial data from a metgrid NetCDF file
to initialize the problem and provide time-dependent boundary conditions.

The inputs_metgrid_slm case initializes the SLM land surface model from the
met_em files: ERF builds the fields real.exe would write to wrfinput (soil
temperature and moisture on the 4 Noah layers, land use and dominant soil
category, skin temperature, and vegetation fraction and LAI interpolated to
the start date from the monthly climatology) and hands them to SLM, which
takes the same path it takes for a wrfinput run. Each level reads its land
state from its own met_em file.

The met_em files in this directory cover only ocean, so this case needs met_em
files for a domain that includes land (see the comments in the inputs file),
along with NoahmpTable.TBL and the four rrtmgp-*.nc files (SLM requires the
radiation model; see Exec/RegTests/WPS_Test/README). Build with USE_RRTMGP=TRUE.
